# Dashboard improvisation conventions

This rule encodes the standards adopted during the PARA dashboard rebuild.
See `docs/VISION.md` for product IA and `docs/PARA.md` for the entity model.

The marketing surfaces already follow this aesthetic — every dashboard page
we touch should match it.

---

## 1. Page layout

Every authenticated page composes the same way:

```tsx
import { PageContainer } from "@/components/shared/page-container"
import { PageHeader } from "@/components/shared/page-header"

export default async function MySurfacePage() {
  // server-side data fetch here
  return (
    <PageContainer width="wide" spacing="default">
      <PageHeader
        eyebrow="Today · Week 12"
        title="Welcome back, Rajon"
        description="A calm look at the week."
        actions={<Button>…</Button>}
      />

      {/* one or more <section> blocks, optionally introduced by <SectionHeader> */}
    </PageContainer>
  )
}
```

- **`<PageContainer>`** owns max-width AND vertical rhythm. Don't manually
  add `space-y-*` on the page root — pass `spacing="compact" | "default" | "generous"`.
- **`<PageHeader>`** is the only allowed page-level title. New code passes
  actions via the `actions` prop; legacy `children` continues to work.
- **`<SectionHeader>`** for in-page section titles (h2). Eyebrow + h2 + optional description + optional actions.
- Width: `wide` (max-w-6xl) for dashboards/lists; `narrow` (max-w-2xl) for forms and detail pages.

---

## 2. Visual primitives — where to import from

| Need | Import |
|---|---|
| Page wrapper (max-width + spacing) | `@/components/shared/page-container` → `<PageContainer>` |
| Page title | `@/components/shared/page-header` → `<PageHeader>` |
| Section title | `@/components/shared/section-header` → `<SectionHeader>` |
| Amber kicker text | `@/components/atmosphere/eyebrow` → `<Eyebrow>` |
| Pro badge glyph | `@/components/atmosphere/pro-mark` → `<ProMark>` |
| Soft animated background (hero areas) | `@/components/atmosphere/soft-backdrop` → `<SoftBackdrop>` |
| Asterisk / seed / enso divider | `@/components/shared/ornament-divider` → `<OrnamentDivider>` |
| Empty state | `@/components/shared/empty-state` → `<EmptyState>` |
| Loading card | `@/components/shared/skeleton-card` → `<SkeletonCard>` |
| Pro gating wrapper | `@/components/upgrade/pro-gate` → `<ProGate>` |
| Standalone Pro upsell card | `@/components/upgrade/pro-upsell-card` → `<ProUpsellCard>` |

Don't re-implement these inline. If a primitive feels wrong for the use case,
**extend the primitive** instead of branching to ad-hoc markup.

---

## 3. Pro / Free gating

- **Source of truth:** `src/lib/config.ts` `planLimits` and `src/lib/plan-access.ts` `hasProProductAccess`.
- **Feature-level helpers:** `src/lib/feature-flags.ts` (`canSeeFullWrapped`, `canSeeAdvancedAnalytics`, `canRunQuarterlyReview`, …). Prefer these over calling `hasProProductAccess` directly so future per-feature divergence is a one-liner.
- **UI gating:** wrap Pro-only content in `<ProGate planTier={…} role={…} feature="…">`. Its default fallback is `<ProUpsellCard>`.
- **Free-at-cap upsell** (e.g. `/anti-goals` Free user at 3/3): render an inline `<ProUpsellCard>` beneath the list. Don't block creation — just nudge.

---

## 4. Data fetching

- Server components by default (`app/(app)/**/page.tsx`).
- Co-locate query helpers under `src/lib/queries/<surface>.ts`. One file per top-level surface (dashboard, goals, daily-habits, analytics, wrapped, …). Each exports a typed function returning **everything that page needs in one call** so we don't N+1 across components.
- Never call `prisma` directly from a component file. Always go through a `lib/queries/*` helper.
- Client components get data via props from their server parent. Never refetch on mount.

---

## 5. Charts (recharts)

Always import from `@/lib/charts-theme`:

```tsx
import {
  chartColors,
  chartSeries,
  axisDefaults,
  gridDefaults,
  tooltipDefaults,
} from "@/lib/charts-theme"
```

- Use `chartColors.amber` for the primary series, `chartColors.ink` for comparison.
- Use `axisDefaults.tick`, `gridDefaults`, `tooltipDefaults` for axes/grids/tooltips.
- Never hardcode HSL values or hex colors in chart configs. The CSS-variable
  references ensure charts re-theme correctly under dark mode.

---

## 6. Motion (framer-motion)

Always import from `@/lib/motion`:

```tsx
import { fadeUp, calmTransition, staggerParent, staggerChild } from "@/lib/motion"
```

- Use `fadeUp` for card / list-item entrances.
- Use `staggerParent` + `staggerChild` for staggered lists.
- Use `easings.calm` (the default in `calmTransition`) for any custom transition.
- Avoid bouncy/elastic/spring easings — they fight the editorial tone.

---

## 7. PARA model — terminology

NBB follows **PARA / Second Brain** (see `docs/PARA.md`):

```
Area  →  Project  →  Task              + Notes & Resources (transversal)
```

Critical naming after Phase 2:

- ❌ **Never** call a `Project` a "Goal" in new code or copy. The Prisma model is `Project`. The URL is `/projects`. The component dir is `src/components/projects/`. The user-facing label is "Project."
- The `Goal` model and `/goals` URL are **deprecated** post-Phase 2 — Prisma keeps DB tables at `goals` via `@@map`, but TypeScript types and code identifiers all read `Project`.
- `LifeCategory` enum stays as-is; it's used as a category *hint* on `Area` (the new entity), not as the area itself.
- The four "task-like" models (`DailySystem`, `KeyResult`, `CheckpointGoal`, `Action`) stay split by intent. UI surfaces them together under "Tasks" in a Project detail.

## 8. What we don't pull in from YIR

- **Echo AI coach** — explicitly out of scope for v1. No `/echo` route, no "coming soon" tease. Revisit post-launch (see `docs/plan/DECISIONS.md` → 2026-05-15 "Skip Echo AI for v1").
- **YIR's localStorage state stores** (`useDrifts`, `useSpine`) — NBB is Prisma + server components. The Quick Capture draft is the only localStorage exception (and it's just a 30-second autosave, not source of truth).
- **YIR's mock data** (`app-mock.ts`, `today-mock.ts`, `wrapped`, etc.) — visual structure only; everything is populated from real Prisma queries via `lib/queries/*`.

> Drift / Quick Capture *did* ship — it's a hybrid textarea + `cmdk` palette. See `docs/plan/DECISIONS.md` → 2026-05-15 "Quick Capture is a hybrid".

If you find yourself wanting to ship a YIR-only mock feature, **stop and add a
note to `PROGRESS.md`'s "Cross-phase follow-ups" section** instead. Do not
ship.

---

## 9. Hard guardrails

- ❌ **No destructive Prisma migrations *outside the planned migration phases*.** New columns must be nullable. New tables fine. The Goal → Project rename (Phase 2) uses `@@map`/`@map` to keep DB tables/columns intact.
- ❌ **No env var or `middleware.ts` changes** unless explicitly approved per-phase. (Phase 5 will add `BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN`.)
- ❌ **No `useSession` on the client to re-derive Pro state** — pass it as a prop from the server parent.
- ❌ **No inline color hex values, no inline HSL.** Always use CSS variables via Tailwind utilities (`text-amber`, `bg-card`, …) or `chartColors`.
- ✅ **`next build` must pass cleanly** at the end of every phase.
- ✅ **One phase = one shippable state.** No half-broken intermediates.

